---
description: Resolve the requested specialist work through current owned identity, original evidence and product history, and choose an authorized local handoff.
budget: { maxTurns: 40 }
args:
  goal: string
returns: SpecialistResult
---
Work toward the actual specialist outcome. Discover the current owned roster and assigned product scope; the focused selection branch can distinguish an intended specialist from an absent, unsuitable or ambiguous one. Choose the candidate investigation, product-history work and continuation from the goal and findings, rather than calling every available helper as a checklist.

The candidate branch can inspect exact current membership, reconcile retained assignments and completions, and read the original artifact. Use actual unavailable, failed, changed or conflicting results to refine the investigation or explain a justified hold. A matching handle is not original worker identity, and a progress message is not completion. Keep provider, task, parent revision and committed source boundaries intact.

When original work is available, the product-history branch can assess its retained contract implications. The handoff decision branch binds a semantic action and explanation to exact observed native identities and bytes. Stage only a requested local integration through the native workspace boundary with the actual required history; preserve its returned artifact. A current permission is not itself a user request. Return the actual application result, including the requested explanation and any retained handoff, without claiming an attempted or proposed action succeeded. No attach, detach, external send, parent merge or parent-source change is in this operation's scope.
